AB  - In this work, we polled 532 professionals from various industries in this study to investigate the relationship between organizational support, business use, decision support frameworks, system complexity, compatibility, and overall usage and stakeholder satisfaction. Some technical parts of the system, including interoperability, have become better, but user satisfaction has kept going down, along with trust in support and decision-making abilities. This set of results illustrates that just upgrading the technology isn't enough to match what customers really want from a data warehouse environment. Instead, the results show that there is a bigger gap between how data warehouse users work on a daily basis and how enterprises are building these systems. © 2026 IEEE.
