TI  - Privacy-Preserving Data Governance and AI Empowerment Platform for Universities Based on 6G Federated Learning
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on 6G: AI-Native Networks, Emerging Technologies, and Future Applications, 6G-ANETA 2026
SP  - 27
EP  - 33
DO  - 10.1145/3828511.3828515
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047268455?origin=resultslist
AB  - To address the contradiction between the growing demand for high-quality educational AI and the strict privacy constraints on cross-campus data sharing, this paper reconstructs the original university data governance and AI empowerment platform into a 6G-enabled federated architecture. The original lakehouse-integrated platform is downgraded into local data sandboxes deployed inside each university or campus, ensuring that core academic affairs, student affairs, research, personnel, and financial records never leave their administrative domains. On top of the local sandboxes, a 6G federated collaboration layer is introduced to support high-bandwidth and ultra-low-latency synchronization of model parameters rather than raw data, thereby enabling LoRA-based Llama 3 8B domain adaptation and privacy-preserving academic early-warning modeling. Building on the original differential privacy mechanism, this paper further evaluates the platform under both 5G and 6G collaborative settings. Experimental results show that, compared with 5G federated collaboration, the 6G scheme reduces average parameter synchronization latency from 128 ms to 41 ms and increases peak synchronization throughput from 612 MB/s to 1865 MB/s, while shortening end-to-end service latency from 103 ms to 91 ms. In addition, the multi-university federated early-warning model achieves an F1-score of 99.41%, outperforming the original single-university baseline of 99.18%, and also exhibits substantially stronger cross-campus generalization under differential privacy constraints of (ℰ =2.8, ⅋ =1×10^-5). The proposed platform demonstrates that 6G can serve as a practical infrastructure for privacy-preserving, data-usable-but-invisible university AI collaboration. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
