AB  - In a context where public and private institutions continuously seek excellence in management and improvement in service delivery, governance is one of the contemporary practices that has been adopted not only as a model for evaluation and monitoring, but also for transparency. To this end, the institutionalization of a governance model represents not only a challenge for public managers, but also the opportunity to make use of information technology, especially Business Intelligence, as a way to ensure agility in accessing and processing information. Through this work, we propose the construction of a prototype of a dashboard for the BI system to be adopted as a practice of governance by results in a Brazilian public institution, focusing on education, not only to support the decision making of managers, but also to allow efficiency and public transparency, and to minimize the difficulties in access, in the management of various BI systems and the informational asymmetries existing in the Public Administration. Copyright © 2021 by SCITEPRESS – Science and Technology Publications, Lda. All rights reserved
