AB  - At the core of clinical informatics is information technology (IT). IT is how the innovative design behind clinical informatics concepts ultimately are presented externally in the real world. For that reason, one must become intimately familiar with what is possible using IT while navigating its boundaries. This chapter will take the reader through ways to represent data, write programs, and conceptualize networks. With some practice, clinical informaticists will understand the trade-offs in various approaches and make the decisions that will produce a reliable IT system for their organization. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2022.
