AB  - This article presents a case study on designing data products, introducing a methodology that guides organizations through each stage of development, from concept to deployment. Key features of data products include governance, marketplace accessibility, global search capabilities, and data discovery, enhancing usability and collaboration. A business knowledge blueprint, similar to a knowledge graph, is used to represent organizational knowledge, capturing relationships between business concepts and incorporating semantic information to enhance the definition of data products and understanding of complex relationships and language within the business. Data contracts, implemented in YAML, outline expectations and standards, facilitating clear communication and integration within the data ecosystem. © 2025 IEEE.
