TI  - Democratizing Data Analytics in Education: A Governance Strategy for Non-Profit Educational Organizations
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of the IEEE Central America and Panama Convention, CONCAPAN
IS  - 2025
DO  - 10.1109/CONCAPAN66820.2025.11512483
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041102512?origin=resultslist
AB  - Implementing a data governance strategy is a complex task, particularly for non-profit organizations (NGOs) facing challenges such as limited resources and expertise gaps. This paper presents a case study on building a data engineering and governance framework for the Ayudinga Foundation, an educational NGO. The work begins with an initial data maturity assessment using the TDWI framework, which revealed a baseline 'Basic' literacy level. Based on this diagnosis, a comprehensive strategy was designed and implemented, including a Data Lakehouse architecture and a formal data governance program. The post-implementation assessment demonstrates a significant improvement, elevating the organization's overall data literacy maturity from 'Basic' (Level 3) to 'Literate' (Level 4). This paper details the methodology, technical implementation, and governance policies, offering a practical blueprint for similar organizations seeking to become data-driven.  © 2025 IEEE.
