AB  - Agile transformation at scale requires architectural strategies to balance modularity, coordination, and enterprise-wide consistency. This study aims to develop a platform-oriented framework that restructures agile development around business-aligned modular components and federated data governance. The framework decomposes software systems into independently managed business components, each tied to specific functional domains and capable of localized development and deployment. These components interact through a centralized internal platform that standardizes infrastructure, tooling, and delivery workflows, enabling consistent integration across distributed teams. To support data consistency and policy compliance across organizational boundaries, the framework adopts a federated governance model inspired by data mesh principles to delegate data ownership to domain teams while preserving interoperability and global oversight. Informed by architectural patterns observed in real-world platform engineering and distributed agile practices, the proposed framework offers a scalable approach for organizations seeking to modernize their agile capabilities while maintaining traceability, modularity, and operational coherence. © 2025 IEEE.
