AB  - With the explosive growth of data volumes and increasing diversity of data types, real-time dynamic data governance has become a critical requirement in data management. This paper proposes an intelligent real-time data governance approach based on lakehouse integration, which decouples the intrinsic functional relationships within data governance, separates data governance from big data platforms, and decouples it from large model platforms. The method establishes a tagging system, constructs data profiles through data exploration, and implements metadata-driven dynamic real-time intelligent data governance. Experimental results demonstrate that this approach effectively enhances the real-time performance and accuracy of data governance while improving data quality. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
