AB  - The term governance comes from the Greek word kubernaein which means ‘to steer.’ Data governance is about governing data management activities (so perhaps data management governance would be a better name). This chapter discusses the definition of data governance, common implementation models, and key roles (data owner, steward, and user). I will show how this comes together in a modern governance structure called data mesh – which ties in with the discussion about data architecture and subject areas in Section 8.2. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
