AB  - Data lineage is a foundational primitive for security, auditing, and compliance in modern lakehouse systems, where large-scale ETL pipelines continuously transform sensitive data. While fine-grained lineage at Parquet row-group granularity is essential for precise root-cause analysis and forensic investigation, naive lineage capture generates massive dependency graphs that are infeasible to store or query at scale. This paper introduces a compressed lineage engine for lakehouse DAGs that enables exact, verifiable row-group provenance with strong security guarantees. The core novelty is a structure-aware compression framework that combines bipartite factoring to reuse repeated parent-set templates with interval packing to compactly encode contiguous dependency patterns, while isolating irregular edges as exceptions to preserve correctness. To ensure lineage integrity and resistance to tampering, the system integrates Merkle-style path hashing, cryptographically binding each row-group's provenance to execution metadata and its upstream dependencies. The resulting design reduces lineage storage by one to two orders of magnitude and supports millisecond-scale root-cause and audit queries without expanding the underlying graph. Experimental evaluation on large synthetic lakehouse DAGs demonstrates that high-resolution, security-aware lineage can be made practical at scale, enabling efficient auditing, impact analysis, and trustworthy data governance. © 2026 IEEE.
