AB  - In activities such as adversarial training and simulated confrontation simulation experiments, a large amount of multi-source heterogeneous data is generated, but these data suffer from problems of difficult management and low utilization. We have built a training experiment big data management and application platform based on the 'resource-service-capability' three-layer logical architecture, which conducts data access and aggregation, cleaning, and standardization, and constructs an experimental theme data warehouse. In response to the actual needs of adversarial training, we adopt the method of 'analysis of variance + multiple linear regression + Apriori algorithm' to carry out analysis from single-factor analysis, multi-factor interaction analysis to spatiotemporal dimension behavior correlation analysis, breaking away from the traditional empirical analysis and comparison mode, and evaluating adversarial training from multiple dimensions. This platform can accurately assess the impact of various factors on training effects, mine the hidden correlation relationships in the behaviors of both adversarial parties, and make accurate predictions about the next behaviors, providing data support for optimizing training programs and offering intelligent decision support to trainers. © 2025 IEEE.
