TI  - Cloud-Native Digital Ecosystem for Construction Cost Intelligence with FL and Cross-Platform Data
PY  - 2026
T2  - Lecture Notes in Electrical Engineering
VL  - 1632 LNEE
SP  - 486
EP  - 499
DO  - 10.1007/978-981-92-0232-4_40
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047328673?origin=resultslist
AB  - Accurate construction cost intelligence is hindered by fragmented data across Building Information Modeling (BIM) platforms, Enterprise Resource Planning (ERP) systems, scheduling tools, Internet of Things (IoT) data streams, and external market indices. This paper presents a cloud-native digital ecosystem that unifies cross-platform data integration with privacy-preserving FL (FL) for cost estimation and risk analytics. The architecture integrates event-driven microservices, a metadata-centric data lakehouse aligned with the Industry Foundation Classes (IFC) ontology, and a zero-trust data plane exposing versioned Application Programming Interfaces (APIs). We formalize cost-intelligence tasks, including unit-price prediction, drift detection, and schedule–cost risk analysis, and design a FL layer that addresses non-independent and identically distributed (non-IID) data, client heterogeneity, and communication efficiency through adaptive client selection, secure aggregation, and optional Differential Privacy (DP). A reference implementation demonstrates end-to-end pipelines, from schema mapping and Change Data Capture (CDC) ingestion to model training, deployment, and monitoring, enabling interoperability across common Architecture, Engineering, and Construction (AEC) toolchains. Evaluation covers accuracy, scalability, and privacy–utility trade-offs, showing that the proposed eco- system enables collaborative cost intelligence without centralizing sensitive project data. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2026.
