AB  - The increasing demand for data-driven clinical decision making from electronic health records (EHRs) requires a standardized framework to guide stakeholders on translating clinical data requirements to technical specifications. The WHO SMART Guidelines was identified to guide translating narrative policies and guidelines into machine-readable specifications, providing structure on how to extract data from an EHR. This framework can help healthcare facilities to systematically process the complexities of EHR adoption as a whole. © 2025 The Authors.
