TI  - Unity Catalog: Open and Universal Governance for the Lakehouse and Beyond
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of the ACM SIGMOD International Conference on Management of Data
SP  - 310
EP  - 322
DO  - 10.1145/3722212.3724459
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105010197888?origin=resultslist
AB  - Enterprises are increasingly adopting the Lakehouse architecture to manage their data assets due to its flexibility, low cost, and high performance. While the catalog plays a central role in this architecture, it remains underexplored, and current Lakehouse catalogs exhibit key limitations, including inconsistent governance, narrow interoperability, and lack of support for data discovery. Additionally, there is growing demand to govern a broader range of assets beyond tabular data, such as unstructured data and AI models, which existing catalogs are not equipped to handle. To address these challenges, we introduce Unity Catalog (UC), an open and universal Lakehouse catalog developed at Databricks that supports a wide variety of assets and workloads, provides consistent governance, and integrates efficiently with external systems, all with strong performance guarantees. We describe the primary design challenges and how UC's architecture meets them, and share insights from usage across thousands of customer deployments that validate its design choices. UC's core APIs and both server and client implementations have been available as open source since June 2024.  © 2025 ACM.
