AB  - Descriptive analytics presents data about what happened in the past, either in textual or graphical form. Predictive analytics builds mathematical models based on past data to predict what might happen in the future and associated probabilities of occurrence (risk). Prescriptive analytics goes beyond predicting what will happen with associated risks of occurrence, it provides some guidance for deciding what can be done about it. More information on the various kinds of analytics is presented in Chapter 25. This chapter focuses on prescriptive analytics in healthcare. This activity is analogous to specification of medical treatments following diagnosis. © 2023 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
