AB  - Exercise and training data is a core asset for enhancing military training and operational decision-making capabilities. Current military exercise and training data faces management challenges such as multi-source heterogeneity, inconsistent standards, and low data quality, which severely restrict its value realization. To address these challenges, this paper designs and implements a data governance system based on big data and data warehouse technologies. This system first constructs a data resource catalog and standard system, utilizing technologies like Flink and HDFS inotify to achieve the aggregation and integration of multi-source heterogeneous data. Through standardized ETL processes and a layered data warehouse, the data undergoes deep processing and organization. Finally, a unified data service and visualization platform supports upper-layer decision-making analysis. Application practices demonstrate that this system significantly improves data standardization, processing efficiency, and analytical capability, providing key technical support for the digital and intelligent transformation of military training. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
