AB  - This paper presents a structured approach to implementing Business Intelligence (BI) within the Brazilian energy market, with the aim of fostering a data-driven culture and improving decision-making processes. The project involved the development of a centralized BI framework, including the standardization of reporting tools, the definition of business metrics (OKRs and KPIs), and the creation of dashboards tailored to strategic, tactical, and operational needs. A new BI cell was proposed to support data governance and self-service analytics, empowering business users with autonomy and agility. A key component of the architecture was the implementation of a corporate data lake, designed to integrate heterogeneous data sources and provide a scalable, flexible foundation for analytics and governance. The methodology included stakeholder participation, a report tree structure, and the establishment of a panel production flow. The results indicate improved data accessibility, increased reporting efficiency, and enhanced insights for commercial and operational strategies. This case study demonstrates how BI and data lake architectures can be effectively structured to support the dynamics of the energy market and organizational intelligence. © 2026 IEEE.
