UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105037871167?origin=resultslist
AB  - Modern analytics environments suffer from persistent metric inconsistency: dashboards, notebooks, and reporting pipelines independently reconstruct business metric definitions, yielding conflicting results that erode trust in data-driven decisions. Existing semantic layer tools remain bound to JavaScript runtimes, proprietary platforms, or specific data-transformation ecosystems, leaving Python-native teams without a unified, open solution. This paper presents SemanticQuark, an open Python-native semantic layer framework that unifies metric definitions, join topology resolution, type-safe schema validation, caching, pre-aggregation, and multi-interface query serving within a single composable system. Join paths are resolved deterministically via breadth-first search over a developer-declared relationship graph. Row-level security is enforced at the semantic model boundary, and pre-aggregation declarations are bound to named semantic entities rather than physical storage artifacts, ensuring portability across heterogeneous database backends. The contribution is one of systems engineering and reference architecture: each constituent technique is established in the literature, but their systematic co-design within a single open Python framework constitutes the original contribution.  © 2013 IEEE.
