AB  - To realize the vision of the Data Mesh, domain experts must be able to manage data directly without relying on technical specialists. Achieving this requires a metadata management approach that is intuitive and lightweight. This paper proposes a conceptual model based on DCAT v3 that streamlines metadata authoring by leveraging the structural relationships among Dataset Series, Versioning, and Manifest fields. By reducing redundancy and complexity in metadata input, the proposed model aims to make DCAT v3 more accessible to non-technical users while maintaining interoperability and continuity across datasets. © 2025 IEEE.
