TI  - Agentic Dashboard Generation from Natural Language on Lakehouse Platforms
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Systems, and Emerging Technologies, ICAISET 2026
DO  - 10.1109/ICAISET66439.2026.11541526
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105042190082?origin=resultslist
AB  - Agentic AI systems are transforming business intelligence (BI) by enabling natural-language-driven generation of analytical artifacts. Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) allow systems to combine reasoning with grounded data access. This paper presents an empirical evaluation of an agentic dashboard generation approach on a lakehouse platform, where natural-language queries are translated into multi-visualization dashboards under governance constraints. We propose a platform-agnostic reference architecture that integrates metadata-aware retrieval, agentic reasoning, and governed execution. The system is evaluated using representative enterprise workloads across financial, sales, and operational analytics, with metrics including task completion, correctness, latency, and robustness. Results show that agentic generation achieves up to 3-5× faster dashboard creation compared to manual workflows, while maintaining acceptable correctness (0.84) and full governance compliance. We further analyze failure modes, including schema ambiguity and metric misinterpretation, and highlight the critical role of metadata quality. The findings demonstrate the feasibility of agentic BI systems while identifying key challenges in accuracy, reproducibility, and reliability for enterprise deployment. © 2026 IEEE.
