AB  - Many IT applications supporting Pharma 4.0 industrialization rely on the complaint management of large data repositories. This case study reviews the validation of big data management of data warehouses, data lakes, and lake-houses. Different database structures and data management are compared with a summary of options for supporting corporate IT infrastructure including dedicated data centers and cloud-based data services. Data governance expectations are outlined including data mapping and data retention. Key compliance considerations are discussed including data integration, GxP data integrity, technology stacks, validation, cloud service providers, AI-enabled applications and tools, and business continuity planning. The case study concludes with a review of inspection readiness. An overview of an example business use case involving digital twins is shared. © 2026 Guy Wingate.
