TI  - Approaching Health Big Data in a federated research context
PY  - 2025
T2  - Convegno Nazionale di Bioingegneria
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105033052365?origin=resultslist
AB  - In today's digital age, organizations are increasingly adopting data-centric architectures, acknowledging data as a crucial and valuable asset. The healthcare sector is no exception, especially in its pursuit of advancing clinical research through the analysis of growing datasets. To achieve this, it is essential to go beyond traditional hospital boundaries and access data from multiple institutions. This paper presents the research of the Italian Health Big Data (HBD) project, suggesting an approach for data sharing in multicentric clinical trials. The proposed framework is built upon: (i) an architecture that extends data lake usage to a federated setting, (ii) essential data governance measures, including data quality, metadata management, and privacy protection, (iii) an evaluation of existing healthcare standards to determine their effectiveness in facilitating data sharing, and (iv) methods for extracting actionable insights from diverse hospital data formats. The contribution describes how different data sources can be standardized through the adoption of pipelines by the research entities with attention to standards for data quality and real interoperability. © 2025 GNB. All Rights Reserved.
