AB  - The proceedings contain 40 papers. The special focus in this conference is on IoT, Intelligent Computing and Security. The topics include: An Infrastructure-Less Communication Platform for Android Smartphones Using Wi-Fi Direct; prioritization in Data Warehouse Requirements—Incorporating Agility; module Allocation Model in Distributed Computing System by Implementing Fuzzy C-means Clustering Technique; a Soft Computing Intelligent Technique Implication for the Comprehensive Audit of Electric Vehicle; A Review About the Design Methodology and Optimization Techniques of CMOS Using Low Power VLSI; Characterization of SPEC2006 Benchmarks Under Multicore Platform to Identify Critical Architectural Aspects; Design of Buck Converter with Modified P&O Algorithm-Based Fuzzy Logic Controller for Solar Charge Controller for Efficient MPPT; DDoS Attack Detection Using Artificial Neural Network on IoT Devices in a Simulated Environment; wearable Location Tracker for Emergency Management; ABBDIoT: Anomaly-Based Botnet Detection Using Machine Learning Model in the Internet of Things Network; a Hybrid Mechanism for Advance IoT Malware Detection; a Cloud-Edge Server-Based Cypher Scheme for Secure Data Sharing in IoT Environment; Attack Detection Based on Machine Learning Techniques to Safe and Secure for CPS—A Review; fake Account Detection in Social Networks with Supervised Machine Learning; peak Detector Circuits for Safeguarding Against Fault Injection Attacks; An Intuitionistic Fuzzy Approach to Analysis Financial Risk Tolerance with MATLAB in Business; deep Learning for Self-learning in Yoga and Fitness: A Literature Review; cardio Vascular Disease Prediction Using Ensemble Machine Learning Techniques; deep Learning Approach for Breast Cancer Detection; A Review of Machine Learning Techniques (MLT) in Health Informatics.
