TI  - Strategic infrastructure modernization in the food industry: Aligning IT architecture with institutional vision
PY  - 2025
T2  - Modernizing the Food Industry: AI-Powered Infrastructure, Security, and Supply Chain Innovation
SP  - 1
EP  - 21
DO  - 10.4018/979-8-3373-5288-6.ch001
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105013948107?origin=resultslist
AB  - The food industry is undergoing a pivotal transformation, driven by evolving consumer expectations, regulatory shifts, and the rapid advancement of digital technologies. Strategic infrastructure modernization-specifically the re-engineering of IT architecture-is at the core of this evolution. This chapter explores how aligning IT infrastructure with institutional vision can unlock new levels of operational efficiency, innovation, and agility. It presents a comprehensive view of modernization strategies, including the adoption of cloud-native platforms, microservices, data lakes, and enterprise integration frameworks tailored to food enterprises. By analyzing real-world cases and technological trends, the chapter underscores the critical role of IT in harmonizing business processes, ensuring regulatory compliance, and enabling data- driven decision-making. The focus is on strategic alignment-where technology not only supports but actively propels business objectives. In doing so, the chapter provides actionable insights for food industry leaders, architects, and IT strategists seeking sustainable digital growth and transformation. © 2026 by IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
