DO  - 10.4018/979-8-3373-0365-9.ch003
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105005128587?origin=resultslist
AB  - Modern data governance would lack a necessary layer of structure and clarity for the large and always- shifting digital information environment without metadata management. Translating as "data about data," the term "metadata" has many uses in many different fields, including healthcare, banking, and e- commerce, where it encourages creativity by improving operational efficiency and compliance. Including procedural, structural, descriptive, and administrative information helps to provide informed decisions, traceability, and interoperability. Including it in contemporary software systems helps to trace data lineage and provide real- time analytics, thereby enhancing data storage, access, and consumption. Metadata is essential for DevSecOps as it helps to match security and compliance with ongoing development cycles. Data mesh and data fabric are two frameworks displaying metadata- driven decentralization that improve analytics and collaboration. Businesses that want to succeed in the digital age and satisfy legal and technological criteria have to be masters in metadata management. © 2025, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
