AB  - Modern enterprise AI and predictive analytics platforms increasingly rely on lakehouse architectures that unify data engineering, analytics, and machine learning workloads. However, governance and metadata management remain significant challenges when legacy Hive-based metastores coexist with modern unified catalog systems. This paper presents a federated metadata architecture that enables incremental migration from Hive Metastore (HMS) environments to a unified governance layer while maintaining operational continuity. The proposed design introduces a read-through federation model, centralized access control, and lineage-aware metadata management without immediate data relocation. We discuss architectural patterns, migration phases, and governance implications, and analyze how this approach enables scalable, secure, and compliant AI analytics in enterprise environments. © 2026 IEEE.
