SP  - 753
EP  - 758
DO  - 10.1145/3778534.3778652
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105027053243?origin=resultslist
AB  - With the rapid digital transformation of the financial industry, data governance has become increasingly critical. Regulatory policies and industry standards have strengthened requirements for classification and grading throughout the data lifecycle. Such mechanisms are not only fundamental to data masking, access control, and compliance auditing, but also form the cornerstone of financial data security governance. This paper proposes FDSRAC-DSPM, an automated classification and grading framework for financial data lakes and warehouses. The framework builds on a hierarchical taxonomy, leverages domain-specific variants generated by large language models to enhance recall, and integrates a Relevance-Aware Classification (RAC) module to refine equivalence judgments through re-ranking. Experiments on both synthetic and real-world financial datasets demonstrate that FDSRAC-DSPM consistently achieves higher precision than multiple reproducible baselines, with stable F1 performance. The proposed approach is practical for deployment and provides financial institutions with a unified methodology for sensitive data classification and grading.  © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
