TI  - Boosting Digital Engineering Workforce Execution With a Semantic Data Fabric
PY  - 2026
T2  - IEEE Aerospace Conference Proceedings
DO  - 10.1109/AERO66936.2026.11519904
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105041408502?origin=resultslist
AB  - The rapid advancement of technology and the increasing complexity of engineering projects necessitate improvements in how systems are developed and acquired. Digital Engineering (DE) addresses these challenges, but workforce development remains an issue. This paper explores how adopting a semantic data fabric enabled with agentic artificial intelligence (AI) can empower the DE workforce by improving data integration, enhancing usability, fostering collaboration, enabling real-time insight, and providing traceability. Previous work is leveraged to illustrate specific intervention points where a semantic data fabric alleviates common issues and boosts workforce execution. To improve data integration, an ontology-first semantic data fabric provides a unified view of data across the engineering lifecycle, eliminating data silos and improving data quality by using standardized vocabularies. This seamless data exchange reduces errors and streamlines processes. To enhance usability, it allows engineers to use their preferred tools, as the semantic layer translates complex data into a common language, making it easier for them to adopt the methodology. The fabric fosters collaboration and better teamwork by creating a shared understanding of data and terminology, which enables cross-functional teams to access and share information easily, accelerating problem-solving. Real-time insights are enabled by real-time data analysis with chatbots and automated data management tasks, which increases productivity and agility. This approach also provides traceability, since a comprehensive record of data lineage is maintained, providing an audit trail for compliance and increasing confidence in the integrity of the engineering process. In conclusion, a semantic data fabric and chatbot offers transformative benefits to the digital engineering workforce to navigate complex projects with greater efficiency and confidence, making it a pivotal tool for effective program execution. © 2026 IEEE.
