AU  - Kahyaoglu, S.B.
AU  - Nzama-Sithole, L.
TI  - From data to decisions: AI, data governance and the future of financial services
PY  - 2026
T2  - AI-Driven Decision-Making in Finance
SP  - 53
EP  - 73
DO  - 10.1201/9781003656463-4
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105048158738?origin=resultslist
AB  - This study is designed to explore the significant impact of analytical capabilities on decision-making processes at all levels within the finance sector, a field increasingly shaped by data-driven dynamics. As the strategic importance of data continues to escalate, this research aims to provide informed policy recommendations for future developments in finance. In this context, the study highlights the critical role of financial institutions in effectively managing risks, identifying market opportunities through competitive analysis, personalizing digital services, and ensuring adherence to regulatory requirements within a highly regulated finance environment. Drawing from a wide variety of data generated in the financial industry, the research seeks to uncover valuable insights into these sophisticated processes. The study specifically addresses the benefits and challenges associated with transitioning from intuitive to data-driven decision-making cultures. While data and data warehouses serve as essential foundations for informed decision-making, they also present challenges, including privacy concerns and the need for skilled professionals. This research emphasizes the evolution of data from mere record-keeping to a sophisticated source of decision-making intelligence. It illustrates how efficient data utilization by financial institutions and markets informs strategic, operational and regulatory decisions. Given the inherent nature of financial institutions and markets, big data is underscored as a vital element in the decision-making process. Furthermore, the study examines the emerging role of artificial intelligence (AI) in enabling real-time big data analytics across various finance fields and services. Ultimately, the study aims to contribute to the existing body of literature by elucidating the developmental path of future financial markets and services, utilizing advanced big data management practices, analytics and AI-based applications. © 2027 Dr. Bilal Bagis.
